So I resumed from hibernation (via tuxonice) (unlikely to be the
problem: this was something like resume #15 without problems). Fifteen
minutes I put some music on. A few minutes later, X stalled and the load
average soared: fifteen seconds later, the stall cleared.  A few minutes
after that, the music stopped and the load started soaring again, with
about 50% CPU time consumed by cpu-sys.

It is not immediately clear to me which subsystem might be responsible.
The kernel log said things suggestive of ALSA or perhaps perf (why is
the PMU kicking in inside ALSA? I'm not running perf at the moment).

