Now the second one (the one which did not clear on its own). This one
isn't stuck inside ALSA/perf, but is suggestive of something to do with
core mm or a seize-up of communication between CPUs (perhaps, guessing
wildly on the grounds that it's new, transparent hugepages are somehow
to blame? it's stuck inside PTE flushing, anyway). To me this suggests
that the tlbstate_lock may have been grabbed and not released, but the
only place this can happen that I can see is being stuck inside
*_wait_icr_idle(), and I have no clue how that might happen.

